{% comment %}
  CartBloom on the cart page.

  A real app block (target: section), unlike the drawer embed. The merchant
  drags this into their cart template and positions it exactly, so there is no
  selector guessing, no MutationObserver, and no overlay to accidentally mount
  behind — all the things that make the drawer hard.

  The host element is rendered here rather than found. The widget script, loaded
  by the app embed, paints into every [data-cartbloom-host] it finds, so this
  block only has to declare where.

  The embed must be enabled for this to do anything: it carries the config and
  the script. That is stated in the block's presence check below rather than
  failing silently.
{% endcomment %}

{%- assign cfg = shop.metafields["$app"]["cartbloom-widget-config"].value -%}

{% if cfg %}
  <div
    data-cartbloom-host
    data-cartbloom-mount="app-block"
    data-cartbloom-placement="cart-page"
    {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
  ></div>
{% else %}
  <!-- CartBloom: cart-page block placed, but no configuration published yet -->
{% endif %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "CartBloom progress bar",
  "target": "section",
  "settings": []
}
{% endschema %}
